  "interpretation": [
    "Product RPC and early-body reuse use the same resident node/exec/AOEM, consensus journal and duplex core.",
    "Only exact pending raw bytes reuse authentication; canonical hash alone cannot bypass changed signature.",
    "Projection lag no longer rejects signature-checked memory admission; exact published parent remains mandatory before selection.",
    "Early bind reuse totals are not before-parent completion totals: new fanout 131/108 versus 2/1; single ingress 146/162 versus 1/1.",
    "Aggregate benefit covers combined scheduling, admission, lookahead and propagation; no single-change causal attribution is proven.",
    "last_error retains parent/context/archive-request rejections. Archive rejection already appears in historical d431a74b binary evidence. Passing recovery does not mean zero diagnostics.",
    "AOEM sibling, legacy and preserved runtime drafts unchanged."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "Two rounds per group on one Windows host, not stable mainnet capacity or four-machine validation.",
    "Single ingress is best effort/non-durable; received and TransactionsTaken are not execution, durable admission or finality.",
    "Offline peer or lost Taken can occupy finite global outbox slots until TTL; fault-condition throughput remains open.",
    "Transport tags 9/10 require peer upgrades; no automatic negotiation. Original tags 1-8 and consensus signed domains unchanged.",
    "V3 wallet signatures retain chain_id domain; transport genesis pins do not provide wallet cross-genesis protection.",
    "Strict first-admission authentication remains on RPC control thread; before-parent overlap is limited in this workload.",
    "Backend aoem_semantic_v2_cpu_callbacks; business GPU, automatic full same-candidate proof and A/A/B on actual product processes remain open.",
    "Experimental native-resident-v1 is not deployment authorization; other product capabilities preserved, not all integrated here.",
    "Pending pool is non-durable; recent receipt query scope 65536. Old data, signing logs, drafts and evidence retained."
  ],
